            <ArticleTitle>[Endocrine and metabolic myocarditis in a young female diabetic with hyperthyroidism (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>703-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 31-year-old female diabetic in hyperthyroidism, after ketoacidosis leading to a hypoglycaemic coma showed diffuse and persistent abnormalities of ventricular repolarization. Arguments are given for myocardial ischemia of metabolic origin by hypersecretion of catecholamines.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
